// `core`'s entry: what `import { … } from "core"` reaches — spec ch37.
//
// **Every file of `core` is a module of its own**, with its own imports and its own scope, as any project's
// files are; this one says which of their names are `core`'s. The compiler carries each file under a key
// no path can spell (`" core/vec.wac"`) and this one under `" core"`, and from there they are read as any
// other files are: lowered, checked, reached and emitted by the same code (`packages/wacc/src/carried.wac`).
//
// A name a file exports and this one does not re-export is shared between `core`'s files and nobody else.
// Everything below was all of `core`'s exports when the files were one concatenated module, which is why
// the lists are as long as they are.

